<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:07:30 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Behind the UK's use of AI in asylum applications</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/behind-the-uk-s-use-of-ai-in-asylum-applications</link><description>
The UK is increasingly turning to artificial intelligence to manage its immigration system, from analysing migrants’ phones to processing asylum applications. But what happens when AI gets involved in deciding how an asylum seeker's story is understood? Stella Elgersma, journalist at InfoMigrants, explains how the UK Home Office is testing AI tools to process asylum applications, including a system that generates summaries of asylum interviews. With errors, limited human oversight and concerns over transparency, could AI put asylum seekers’ lives at risk?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e36442a-e428-11f1-a386-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-143639-144049-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e36442a-e428-11f1-a386-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-143639-144049-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33d74b0e-e428-11f1-8380-35699edb96b7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:07:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>China summit ends with little new, Europe backs Ukraine in Berlin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin</link><description>
The leaders of China, the United States and Russia met in Shenzhen for a historic first, but the summit brought little new: non-binding statements on peace and no plan to meet regularly. In Berlin, Europeans gathered to show their support for Ukraine, a pointed answer to a summit where Europe had no seat, as FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf9490a-e41f-11f1-8a6b-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-140128-140711-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf9490a-e41f-11f1-8a6b-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-140128-140711-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f3513e08-e41f-11f1-ae06-0db31b1ab018</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:04:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine's European allies meet in Berlin in show of support</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-s-european-allies-meet-in-berlin-in-show-of-support</link><description>
Ukraine’s main European allies are meeting in Berlin on Thursday as a show of support for Kyiv, with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner also attending. The gathering, which brings together the leaders of Germany, France, Britain, Poland and Italy as well as NATO chief Mark Rutte, takes place as Trump and Putin meet in China, fuelling fears in Europe that decisions on the war could be made without its input. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Germany has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3999d8f4-e21b-11f1-8b8b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316805802362.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3999d8f4-e21b-11f1-8b8b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316805802362.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8491ffc-e400-11f1-9722-0f0809d6071d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:43:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Denmark ratifies Greenland security deal after months of pressure by Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-denmark-ratifies-greenland-security-deal-after-months-of-pressure-by-trump</link><description>
Denmark's parliament on Thursday ratified a security deal involving Greenland and the United States. The vote comes months after the US, Denmark and Greenland ​signed the ‌agreement to end a standoff with the Trump administration over the Arctic island's future. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/337a8fc4-e3fe-11f1-82a1-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266587574802.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/337a8fc4-e3fe-11f1-82a1-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266587574802.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2324459e-e3fd-11f1-81b8-d3313f191154</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:08:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/337a8fc4-e3fe-11f1-82a1-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26266587574802.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin to rally support for Kyiv after Trump-Putin-Xi talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-european-leaders-to-meet-in-berlin-to-support-for-ukraine-after-trump-putin-xi-talks</link><description>
Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin on Thursday to shore up support for Kyiv just hours after Russia's Vladimir Putin took part in a historic trilateral meeting with US President Donald Trump and China's Xi Jinping. The "Coalition of the Willing" summit comes as Europe is hoping to secure a seat at the table of any future peace talks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92fca864-e41d-11f1-980c-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26323457805562.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92fca864-e41d-11f1-980c-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26323457805562.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8c83dce-e3c4-11f1-a73b-116921ae379c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:55:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92fca864-e41d-11f1-980c-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26323457805562.jpg">© Bernd von Jutrczenka, DPA via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>COP31: Vanuatu calls for UN climate summit reform, warns of backsliding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding</link><description>
Vanuatu's Environment Minister Ralph Regenvanu has called for changes to the UN climate summit process, accusing a small group of countries of blocking progress and warning that COP31 risks reversing previous commitments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8e0060-e3d0-11f1-9616-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7VU8WE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8e0060-e3d0-11f1-9616-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7VU8WE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5df44426-e3bc-11f1-be92-6d9f3ae22326</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:00:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8e0060-e3d0-11f1-9616-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7VU8WE.jpg">© Yasin Akgul, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Crimea bridge strike: Fact-checking fake videos of damage after Ukraine's attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261118-crimea-bridge-strike-fact-checking-fake-videos-of-damage-after-ukraine-s-attack</link><description>
Ukraine struck the Kerch Bridge linking Russia to occupied Crimea, but not all the dramatic footage circulating online is real. Multiple AI-generated videos falsely show the bridge collapsed with extensive damage. Some even used branding resembling a Ukrainian news agency to appear credible. While the bridge was indeed struck and damaged, the viral videos were fabricated using AI, as Vedika Bahl explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5b1bea-e39a-11f1-83bd-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/kerch.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5b1bea-e39a-11f1-83bd-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/kerch.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ed05ade-e39a-11f1-8df1-35772d82a0de</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:51:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Why Ukraine keeps trying to bring down Russia's bridge to Crimea</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-why-ukraine-keeps-trying-to-bring-down-russia-s-bridge-to-crimea</link><description>
A Ukrainian drone and missile strike on Monday night brought down a stretch of the bridge linking the annexed Crimean Peninsula to Russia, potentially crippling a route long used by Moscow to move men and materiel into Crimea and the southern front. Here’s why Kyiv keeps testing its strength against an infrastructure project that has become synonymous with Russian President Vladimir Putin’s 2014 seizure of the peninsula.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b1cf78a-e374-11f1-ae39-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-17T132708Z-373589621-RC2PPOA5FXQR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-CRIMEA-SBU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b1cf78a-e374-11f1-ae39-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-17T132708Z-373589621-RC2PPOA5FXQR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-CRIMEA-SBU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f055bd98-e373-11f1-a1da-21f28020077c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:17:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b1cf78a-e374-11f1-ae39-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-17T132708Z-373589621-RC2PPOA5FXQR-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-CRIMEA-SBU.jpg">© Security Service of Ukraine handout via Reuters</source><dc:creator>Paul MILLAR</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>War in Ukraine: Is France in direct conflict with Russia?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-war-in-ukraine-is-france-in-direct-conflict-with-russia</link><description>
An investigation published by the French public radio channel RFI on November 17 revealed that a confidential mission by the French army known as "Volia" has been used for months to conceal the presence of French personnel in Ukraine. Russia was prompt to accuse France of direct involvement in the conflict. Is this true?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8cecea6e-e36a-11f1-b640-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/French-troops-Ukraine-10.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8cecea6e-e36a-11f1-b640-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/French-troops-Ukraine-10.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d1857d58-e36a-11f1-b037-f9b6f7051788</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:57:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia’s new low-cost munitions pose a fresh threat to Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-russia-new-low-cost-munitions-threat-ukraine</link><description>
Dan-T, Filin and Geran-5 might not mean anything to you, but in Ukraine, everyone is talking about these munitions. These new Russian weapons are small, fast and cheap – and a major threat, as they were specially designed to get around Ukrainian anti-aircraft defences and strike deep within the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87fb8c48-ddf9-11f1-b48e-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/cou1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87fb8c48-ddf9-11f1-b48e-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/cou1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">050fc2a8-e35e-11f1-a42e-57ba12ee4c8d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:19:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87fb8c48-ddf9-11f1-b48e-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/cou1.jpg">© Telegram / UA_National_Police</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU proposes new €45 billion Ukraine loan to be repaid by Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-eu-proposes-new-%E2%82%AC45-billion-ukraine-loan-to-be-repaid-by-russia</link><description>
European Commission President Ursula von ⁠der Leyen announced on Wednesday a proposed €45 billion loan to Ukraine for 2027 to help cover around two-thirds ​of Kyiv's financing ​needs. The loan will be repaid ⁠through future ⁠war reparations by Russia, von der Leyen added. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5199c72-e338-11f1-83de-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T100455Z-260316918-RC29QOAC9KFB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-EU-LOAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5199c72-e338-11f1-83de-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T100455Z-260316918-RC29QOAC9KFB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-EU-LOAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c432c534-e338-11f1-b6c6-d1632dd8ccd0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:42:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5199c72-e338-11f1-83de-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T100455Z-260316918-RC29QOAC9KFB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-EU-LOAN.jpg">© Yves Herman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Italy approves anti-semitism law despite concerns over freedom of expression</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-italy-approves-anti-semitism-law-despite-concerns-over-freedom-of-expression</link><description>
Italy's ​parliament on Tuesday approved a new bill aimed at combating anti-semitism – which lists some forms of criticism of ⁠Israel as examples of anti-semitic conduct – despite concerns that it could limit freedom of expression and advocacy for Palestinian rights. The law will not impose financial ⁠penalties or criminal sanctions for offenders.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ca81bd0-e321-11f1-98b5-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321718278404.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ca81bd0-e321-11f1-98b5-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321718278404.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c96e07c4-e320-11f1-a713-d7983421cd50</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:37:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ca81bd0-e321-11f1-98b5-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321718278404.jpg">© Alessandra Tarantino, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Authorities take over Turkey's last pro-opposition broadcaster Sozcu TV</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/authorities-take-over-turkey-s-last-pro-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv</link><description>
Police raided the Istanbul headquarters of Sozcu TV on Tuesday, dealing another significant blow to Turkey's pro-opposition media. This is the third such seizure of pro-opposition media in just over a year. It comes amid public uproar over a multi-billion investment fund scandal that has affected the savings of nearly half a million people and piled pressure on President Recep Tayyip Erdogan's ruling AKP party ahead of elections in 2028. FRANCE 24's Jasper Mortimer reports from Ankara.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6178ba6-e2c0-11f1-ac75-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-203821-204220-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6178ba6-e2c0-11f1-ac75-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-203821-204220-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb93c162-e2c0-11f1-91c1-0bffe5cc4ef6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:58:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Estonia closes its border with Russia but can it keep Moscow out?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-estonia-closes-its-border-with-russia-but-can-it-keep-moscow-out</link><description>
Estonia announced this weekend it would close its border with Russia, after blaming its eastern neighbour of attempting to sabotage one of its drone factories. But at a time when the internet has become one of Russia’s most potent weapons to wage hybrid warfare, does closing the border even matter?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/638675fe-e1d1-11f1-97ac-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/russie-estonie-frontiere.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/638675fe-e1d1-11f1-97ac-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/russie-estonie-frontiere.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">279c2752-e297-11f1-94a5-0152eee4ccc8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:28:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/638675fe-e1d1-11f1-97ac-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/russie-estonie-frontiere.png">© Studio graphique France Médias Monde</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine: Two bridges in Kyiv heavily damaged by Russian strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261117-ukraine-two-bridges-in-kyiv-heavily-damaged-by-russian-strikes</link><description>
Russia hit two major bridges in Kyiv while Ukraine struck Moscow's link to annexed Crimea for the second night in a row, officials said Tuesday, ahead of a historic meeting of Chinese, US and Russian leaders. Detals from the ground by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3345e766-e281-11f1-be99-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-Ukraine-bridge0.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3345e766-e281-11f1-be99-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-Ukraine-bridge0.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">866461ac-e281-11f1-9313-27c571c83991</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:54:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Data leak exposes Deutsche Bank ties to Russian oligarchs, Epstein and Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261117-deutsche-bank-shares-drop-after-reports-on-mass-data-leak</link><description>
Shares in Deutsche Bank plunged Tuesday after international media outlets published reports detailing the bank's questionable business practices over the past 20 years, including its ties to Russian oligarchs, convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein and Donald Trump before he became the US president.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d39c8d8-e26b-11f1-8a0d-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/6597867e619fbec5d361e81bac59edcd25bf3247.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d39c8d8-e26b-11f1-8a0d-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/6597867e619fbec5d361e81bac59edcd25bf3247.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ec6458c-e26b-11f1-a59d-11625b95354e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:45:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d39c8d8-e26b-11f1-8a0d-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/6597867e619fbec5d361e81bac59edcd25bf3247.jpg">© Kirill Kudryavtsev, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine critically damages bridge linking occupied Crimea with Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-ukraine-critically-damages-bridge-linking-occupied-crimea-with-russia</link><description>
Ukrainian drones and missiles struck a vital bridge linking Russia to the occupied Crimean Peninsula, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Tuesday, calling it an “unprecedented” operation as Russia reported that its forces downed a record number of Ukrainian drones for the second straight day. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b2e5ce16-e27a-11f1-afcd-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/fb95ba6b20b42f267fa8e79df5f7c45527b7e136.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b2e5ce16-e27a-11f1-afcd-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/fb95ba6b20b42f267fa8e79df5f7c45527b7e136.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2fab9620-e252-11f1-8feb-85a6155a7499</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:43:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b2e5ce16-e27a-11f1-afcd-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/fb95ba6b20b42f267fa8e79df5f7c45527b7e136.jpg">© Handout Ukrainian security service via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Putin arrives in China ahead of trilateral Trump-Xi summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-live-russian-attacks-target-bridges-in-kyiv-knocking-out-heating-and-water-ukraine</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday arrived in China where he is expected to meet with his US and Chinese counterparts Donald Trump and Xi Jinping on the sidelines of the APEC summit, Russian state media reported. Russian state news agency TASS said that Putin's plane has landed at Shenzhen's Bao'an International Airport. Putin will take part in the summit later this week. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcf47c90-e2c3-11f1-a3fd-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321697934960.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcf47c90-e2c3-11f1-a3fd-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321697934960.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84e4ae92-e220-11f1-9cd9-b1b6d1450501</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:38:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcf47c90-e2c3-11f1-a3fd-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321697934960.jpg">© Anupam Nath, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russian strikes hit two key bridges in Kyiv, disrupting water and power supplies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-russian-strikes-hit-two-key-bridges-in-kyiv-disrupting-water-and-power-supplies-ukraine</link><description>
